# _identity.env — UPSTREAM-IDENTITY drift oracle for the ANGULAR-HOST archetype.
#
# EXEMPLAR MEMBER = the native-federation host shell, published as
# `hugmesh-host-shell` (repos[].name `host-shell`), resolved by the normal
# pull-repo-base.sh lookup; HOST_SHELL_BASE_DIR / --base are offline overrides.
#
# These are the ORIGINAL literal token values the archetype recipe carries in
# the READ-ONLY upstream base. NOT secrets, NOT tenant brand — the base's own
# identity, read from `git show origin/main:` on the exemplar. NOTE:
# BRAND_TITLE here is the WHOLE site title, because the host tab-title anchor
# rebrands the entire <title> — unlike the spring-bff/angular-mfe oracles where
# BRAND_TITLE is the leading word of a longer per-UI title. On the exemplar the
# whole title is exactly the bare brand word ("HugMesh"), so the two forms
# coincide here; the anchor is still whole-title by construction.
#
# scripts/validate-repo-templates.sh renders each recipe anchor's find + replace
# AND the class-A .hbs with these values and asserts anchored-region drift:
#   (1) find@upstream still occurs in the freshly-pulled base
#   (2) replace@upstream == find@upstream (round-trip no-op)
#   (3) each class-A whole-file .hbs renders byte-identical to the base file
#
# NOT consumed at emit time — the driver derives REAL tenant values. Oracle only.
BRAND_TITLE="HugMesh"
HOST_NAME="hugmesh-host"
GENERATOR_ORG_GROUP="hugmesh/hugmesh-generator"
